{:edb/db-before-t 2237 :edb/db-after-t 2238 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535550 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:22:28.105Z" 13194139535550 true] [17592186354860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354861 13194139535550 false] [17592186354860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354874 13194139535550 true] [17592186354860 1100 "Determine whether a differentiable classical solution on an open interval containing the initial point exists for the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139535550 true] [17592186354860 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139535550 false] [17592186354860 1145 "A classical solution must be differentiable on an interval containing $x=1$ and satisfy the differential equation at that point. Substituting $x=1$ and $y(1)=1$ gives\n\n$$\\left(\\frac{1}{1\\cdot1}-\\frac11\\right)y'(1)=2,\\qquad 0\\cdot y'(1)=2.$$\n\nThis is impossible for a finite derivative. Therefore no differentiable classical solution exists for the stated initial condition.\n\nFormal separation on nonsingular regions gives\n\n$$(1/y-1)\\,dy=2x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|-y=x^2+C.$$\n\nRequiring the integrated level set to contain $(1,1)$ yields $C=-2$, hence $\\ln|y|-y=x^2-2$. This is the source's formally integrated relation, but it is not a classical solution of the IVP. Differentiating it at $(1,1)$ again requires $0\\cdot y'(1)=2$. Near $y=1$, continuity would give $y>0$, and $\\ln y-y\\le -1$ makes $x^2\\le1$ necessary on that level set, so it cannot supply a graph on a two-sided neighborhood of $x=1$ either.\n\nThe source capture and its accepted formal relation are retained for provenance. The corrected study answer concerns the original IVP's existence." 13194139535550 true] [17592186354860 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$" 13194139535550 false] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354862 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354863 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354864 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354865 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354866 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354875 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1041 "selection" 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354875 13194139535550 true] [17592186354874 1110 #uuid "dc7ecdf4-9edf-52dc-b394-d454fba788f6" 13194139535550 true] [17592186354875 1034 "No differentiable classical solution exists." 13194139535550 true] [17592186354875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535550 true] [17592186354875 1111 #uuid "a0b3dbd0-63f9-594d-94cb-6b783e0bc8a9" 13194139535550 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection" 17592186354874 "q-104058/singular-ivp-v1/selection/correct-answer" 17592186354875} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
